# Expo Ultimate Starter — Cursor Agent Rules

You are working in a production-ready React Native Expo AI starter kit.
Follow these rules strictly. Prefer small, focused diffs over rewrites.

## Stack (do not replace without explicit user request)

- Expo SDK 57 + Expo Router (file-based routing)
- TypeScript (strict)
- NativeWind v4 + Tailwind CSS 3.4 (`className` styling)
- Lucide React Native icons
- Supabase auth (`lib/supabase.ts`, `context/AuthContext.tsx`)
- Google Gemini via REST (`lib/ai.ts`)

## TypeScript rules

1. Always use strict TypeScript. No `any` unless unavoidable and justified in a one-line comment.
2. Prefer explicit return types on exported functions and hooks.
3. Colocate domain types near usage, or add shared types under `types/`.
4. Env vars must be typed in `types/env.d.ts` and only accessed as `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_*`.
5. Prefer `unknown` + narrowing over loose casts.
6. Keep Expo Router typed routes enabled (`experiments.typedRoutes` in `app.json`). Use `Href` / typed `router.push` paths.

## NativeWind / styling constraints

1. Style with NativeWind `className` only. Avoid `StyleSheet.create` unless a library API requires style objects (e.g. tabBarStyle).
2. Use the project palette: deep slate (`slateink-*`) + teal accent (`brand-*`). Support light and dark (`dark:` variants).
3. Do not introduce purple/indigo “AI slop” themes, neon glow spam, or emoji-as-UI.
4. Keep layouts calm and high-converting: clear hierarchy, generous spacing, rounded-2xl/3xl surfaces, minimal chrome.
5. New Tailwind tokens belong in `tailwind.config.js` — do not hardcode one-off hex values when a token exists.
6. Import `global.css` only from `app/_layout.tsx`.

## Expo Router structure (do not break)

```
app/
  _layout.tsx          # AuthProvider + ThemeProvider + root Stack
  index.tsx            # Auth redirect gate
  (auth)/
    _layout.tsx
    login.tsx
    register.tsx
  (tabs)/
    _layout.tsx        # Dashboard / AI Assistant / Paywall tabs
    index.tsx
    ai-assistant.tsx
    paywall.tsx
```

Rules for agents:

1. Never move auth or tab routes outside their groups without updating redirects in `app/index.tsx`, `(auth)/_layout.tsx`, and `(tabs)/_layout.tsx`.
2. New authenticated screens go under `app/(tabs)/` or a new protected group with a layout guard.
3. New public/auth screens go under `app/(auth)/`.
4. Shared UI goes in `components/`; business logic in `lib/`; providers in `context/`.
5. Do not reintroduce `App.tsx` as the entry — `package.json` main is `expo-router/entry`.
6. Preserve bottom tabs: Dashboard, AI Assistant, Paywall/Settings.

## Architecture conventions

1. Auth only through `useAuth()` from `context/AuthContext.tsx`.
2. Theme only through `useTheme()` from `context/ThemeContext.tsx`.
3. AI calls only through `lib/ai.ts` (never call Gemini URLs directly from screens).
4. Supabase client only from `lib/supabase.ts`.
5. Keep screens presentational where possible; extract reusable pieces into `components/`.
6. Handlers must be functional (no TODO stubs). If a third-party service is missing, degrade gracefully with clear user messaging (demo auth / demo AI / Alert for IAP).

## Quality bar

1. Run `npm run typecheck` after substantive changes.
2. Do not add placeholder “Coming soon” screens when the user asked for working UI.
3. Prefer Expo-compatible packages (`npx expo install …`).
4. Avoid unnecessary `useMemo` / `useCallback` unless stabilizing expensive work or dependency-sensitive APIs.
5. Match existing naming: PascalCase components, camelCase functions, kebab-case route files.

---

## Boilerplate prompts (paste into Cursor to generate sub-pages in < 60s)

### 1) New authenticated settings sub-page

```
Create app/(tabs)/settings.tsx as a Settings screen using NativeWind (slateink + brand palette) and Lucide icons.
Include sections: Profile summary from useAuth(), theme toggle via useTheme(), Sign out button, and links row.
Register it in app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx as a fourth tab OR hide it from the tab bar and navigate from Dashboard.
Use TypeScript, no StyleSheet, no stubs. Keep Expo Router group structure intact.
```

### 2) New AI tool page (summarizer)

```
Add app/(tabs)/summarizer.tsx: a NativeWind form with a multiline input, tone selector (neutral/friendly/executive), and a result panel.
On submit, call streamChatCompletion from lib/ai.ts with a system-style instruction baked into the user prompt.
Show streaming text updates. Add a tab or Dashboard quick-action to open it. Strict TypeScript, Lucide icons, light/dark support.
```

### 3) Auth-gated modal feature

```
Create app/modal-feedback.tsx as a stack modal screen (register in app/_layout.tsx with presentation: 'modal').
Form: rating 1–5, message TextField, submit Button. On submit Alert success and router.back().
Guard with useAuth(); if no session, Redirect to /(auth)/login. NativeWind only, match existing UI components in components/ui.
```

### 4) Paywall feature flag card

```
Update app/(tabs)/paywall.tsx to add a third enterprise tier card ($199/yr) with a feature checklist and selected-state border using brand-500.
Keep monthly/annual toggle working for existing tiers. Upgrade/Restore handlers must remain functional (Alert stubs OK). No purple theme.
```

### 5) Reusable empty state component

```
Create components/ui/EmptyState.tsx accepting title, description, actionLabel?, onAction?.
Use Lucide Inbox icon, NativeWind classes, and dark mode. Use it in the AI Assistant when messages length is 0 after clearing chat.
Export clean props types. Do not modify unrelated files.
```

### 6) Supabase profile fetch hook

```
Create hooks/useProfile.ts that reads the current user from useAuth() and returns { email, displayName, initials }.
Use it on the Dashboard header. Strict TypeScript, no any, no new dependencies.
```
